<title>UK: NWE oil, gas rigs fall three to 65 in latest week.</title>
<headline>NWE oil, gas rigs fall three to 65 in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs operating in offshore Northwest Europe (NWE) fell to 65 in the week ending April 16, down from 68 the previous week, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>The number of rigs in U.K. waters fell by four to 30 while Norwegian rigs gained one to 19. The Danish sector was unchanged at five rigs and the Dutch sector was down one at 10. Ireland boasted one rig from zero.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
